{# IN·14 — how many of this window's incidents REACHED each state.

   Reached, not "are sitting in": a resolved incident passed through
   verification, so it counts on the verified row. Conflating the two would draw
   a funnel that widens, which is the one shape a funnel cannot have
   ({@see IncidentDashboard::reachedCounts}).

   THE DRAWING IS THE ATLAS'S, and the order is what keeps the funnel a funnel:
   the states are stated in the order the workflow runs them. #}
<div class="c" data-w="funnel">
    {{ atlas_chart(dashboard.funnelChart, 'Status funnel') }}
</div>
